From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Alef <chris@crickertech.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 02:21:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Let Kani target riscv64gc-unknown-linux-gnu from an aarch64
 or x86_64 host

Carried by nife (https://github.com/crickertech/nife) in
patches/kani-0.67.0-riscv64-target.patch, against the kani-0.67.0 tag,
under nife's DECISIONS section 218 (provisional number) and milestone 589.
nife builds Kani from that release tag plus this file, never from a fork.

What it does. CBMC is host-independent and already models riscv64
(set_arch_spec_riscv64 in src/util/config.cpp), so what Kani lacks is a
riscv64 target, not a riscv64 host. Four places tie Kani to its host:

- compiler_interface.rs new_machine_model: a riscv64 arm (the aarch64
  arm with the RISC-V psABI's signed 32-bit wchar_t and binary128 long
  double; char is unsigned on both).
- compiler_interface.rs check_target: admit riscv64-unknown-linux-gnu.
- compiler_interface.rs target_config: report riscv64gc's features, so
  rustc does not warn "target feature `d` must be enabled to ensure that
  the ABI of the current target can be implemented correctly" on every
  crate (measured: 54 warnings on nife's kernel without it, 0 with it).
- kani-driver (call_cargo.rs, cov_session.rs) and tools/build-kani
  (sysroot.rs): read the target from KANI_TARGET instead of env!("TARGET").
  build-kani reads it at build time (option_env!), so a build made with
  KANI_TARGET set has a riscv64-only sysroot; the driver reads it at run
  time. KANI_TARGET is a provisional name, and upstream's is upstream's
  to choose.

Where it goes upstream. model-checking/kani#2402, "Command-line flag to
change model target or environment". A separate nife lane reworks this
into an upstream-shaped -Z flag with a multi-target sysroot; this carried
file deliberately stays the minimal tested shape.

When to delete it. When nife's Kani pin reaches a release containing
riscv64 target support: delete this file, its patches/README.md entry,
script/verify-riscv64's build step, and the cache step in verify.yml's
`prove the kernel on riscv64` job. Rebase it (and rename it for the new
version) whenever the pin moves before then.

When to revisit carrying it. Switch to a maintained fork only if the
carried change grows past a few hundred lines, or nife comes to carry
several Kani patches at once. Below that line a single patch file is
cheaper to read, rebase and delete than a fork is to keep in step.
---
 .../compiler_interface.rs                     | 37 +++++++++++++++++++
 kani-driver/src/call_cargo.rs                 |  9 ++++-
 kani-driver/src/coverage/cov_session.rs       |  5 ++-
 tools/build-kani/src/sysroot.rs               |  2 +-
 4 files changed, 48 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kani-compiler/src/codegen_cprover_gotoc/compiler_interface.rs b/kani-compiler/src/codegen_cprover_gotoc/compiler_interface.rs
index 845eb45..009e177 100644
--- a/kani-compiler/src/codegen_cprover_gotoc/compiler_interface.rs
+++ b/kani-compiler/src/codegen_cprover_gotoc/compiler_interface.rs
@@ -307,6 +307,11 @@ fn target_config(&self, sess: &Session) -> TargetConfig {
                 // AArch64 mandates Neon support
                 _ => vec![sym::neon],
             }
+        } else if sess.target.arch == Arch::RiscV64 {
+            // riscv64gc: the lp64d ABI needs `d` (and `d` implies `f`). Without this rustc warns
+            // "target feature `d` must be enabled to ensure that the ABI of the current target can
+            // be implemented correctly" on every crate, a warning it says will become an error.
+            ["m", "a", "f", "d", "c", "zicsr", "zifencei"].map(Symbol::intern).to_vec()
         } else {
             vec![]
         };
@@ -572,8 +577,11 @@ fn check_target(session: &Session) {
     let is_x86_64_darwin_target = session.target.llvm_target.starts_with("x86_64-apple-");
     // looking for `arm64-apple-*`
     let is_arm64_darwin_target = session.target.llvm_target.starts_with("arm64-apple-");
+    // riscv64gc Linux (LP64D), reached from another host through KANI_TARGET.
+    let is_riscv64_linux_target = session.target.llvm_target == "riscv64-unknown-linux-gnu";
 
     if !is_x86_64_linux_target
+        && !is_riscv64_linux_target
         && !is_arm64_linux_target
         && !is_x86_64_darwin_target
         && !is_arm64_darwin_target
@@ -884,6 +892,35 @@ fn new_machine_model(sess: &Session) -> MachineModel {
                 word_size: int_width,
             }
         }
+        Arch::RiscV64 => {
+            // RISC-V psABI, LP64D: char is unsigned, wchar_t is a signed int,
+            // long double is IEEE binary128.
+            let int_width = 32;
+            MachineModel {
+                // CBMC's config.cpp set_arch() accepts "riscv64".
+                architecture: "riscv64".to_string(),
+                alignment,
+                bool_width: 8,
+                char_is_unsigned: true,
+                char_width: 8,
+                double_width: 64,
+                float_width: 32,
+                int_width,
+                is_big_endian,
+                long_double_width: 128,
+                long_int_width: 64,
+                long_long_int_width: 64,
+                memory_operand_size: int_width / 8,
+                null_is_zero: true,
+                pointer_width,
+                rounding_mode: RoundingMode::ToNearest,
+                short_int_width: 16,
+                single_width: 32,
+                wchar_t_is_unsigned: false,
+                wchar_t_width: 32,
+                word_size: int_width,
+            }
+        }
         _ => {
             panic!("Unsupported architecture: {architecture}");
         }
diff --git a/kani-driver/src/call_cargo.rs b/kani-driver/src/call_cargo.rs
index fbcd09c..27023f1 100644
--- a/kani-driver/src/call_cargo.rs
+++ b/kani-driver/src/call_cargo.rs
@@ -133,7 +133,7 @@ pub fn cargo_build_std(&self, std_path: &Path, krate_path: &Path) -> Result<Vec<
 
     /// Calls `cargo_build` to generate `*.symtab.json` files in `target_dir`
     pub fn cargo_build(&mut self, keep_going: bool) -> Result<CargoOutputs> {
-        let build_target = env!("TARGET"); // see build.rs
+        let build_target: &str = &kani_target(); // see build.rs
         let metadata = self.cargo_metadata(build_target)?;
         let target_dir = self
             .args
@@ -475,7 +475,7 @@ fn packages_to_verify<'b>(
 pub fn cargo_config_args() -> Vec<CargoArg> {
     [
         "--target",
-        env!("TARGET"),
+        Box::leak(kani_target().into_boxed_str()),
         // Propagate `--cfg=kani_host` to build scripts.
         "-Zhost-config",
         "-Ztarget-applies-to-host",
@@ -656,3 +656,8 @@ fn package_targets(args: &VerificationArgs, package: &Package) -> Vec<Verificati
     }
     verification_targets
 }
+
+/// The triple Kani compiles for: KANI_TARGET if set, otherwise the host Kani was built for.
+pub fn kani_target() -> String {
+    std::env::var("KANI_TARGET").unwrap_or_else(|_| env!("TARGET").to_string())
+}
